## Typed FFI returns — Mutex chain.
##
## Source: docs/specs/types/typed_ffi_returns.spec.md (B6).
##
## Verifies the end-to-end Mutex surface lifts through typeck:
##   let m = Mutex.new(10)    # m: Mutex[Int]   (B1+B3)
##   let g = m.lock_raw       # g: MutexGuard[Int]  (B5: lib-decl `-> MutexGuard[T]` substituted)
##   let v = g.get            # v: Int            (B4: T resolved from MutexGuard[Int])
##
## Pre-typed-FFI-returns (commits before this spec), `m.lock_raw` would
## report `Int` (the lib decl said `-> Int`) and `g.get` would error
## with "no field `get` on type `Int`" at typeck. The fix in
## `library/std/sync/src/lib.rx` declares structured return types;
## `subst_ty` in `typeck/infer.rs` recurses into `Ty::Class` so the
## generic args substitute end-to-end.

def main
  let m = Mutex.new(10)
  let g = m.lock_raw
  let v = g.get
  if v == 10
    puts "ok"
  else
    puts "fail"
  end
end
